   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Four routines, each doing one job.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`sweep()`** is the workhorse: step the generator across a list of frequencies, keep the\n",
    "receiver pinned exactly on the drive, and read a complex number at each point. Because the\n",
    "receiver is at DC the result is coherent — it carries **amplitude and phase**, which matters\n",
    "because Step 5 gets a second, independent width out of the phase alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`fit_lorentzian()`** turns amplitude-versus-frequency into a centre and a width. The trick\n",
    "that makes it need no fitting library: the *reciprocal* of a Lorentzian power curve is a\n",
    "parabola in frequency, so an ordinary weighted quadratic fit recovers everything. The\n",
    "complication it has to handle is a **baseline**. `1/p` is a parabola only for a *pure*\n",
    "Lorentzian; any additive floor is absorbed into the parabola and inflates the fitted width —\n",
    "negligible where the peak towers over the floor, severe where it does not. On a bench coil\n",
    "behind 0.3 pF the floor will not be negligible, so the baseline is found by search rather than\n",
    "assumed to be zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`width_from_phase()`** is the independent check. A resonator's phase swings through 180°\n",
    "across its line, passing ±45° exactly one half-linewidth either side of centre. So the\n",
    "distance between the ±45° crossings *is* the linewidth. Crucially it uses **no amplitude\n",
    "information at all**, so a sloping baseline, a wrong gain, or a slow drift in drive level\n",
    "cannot move it. Any fixed cable delay adds a straight slope to the phase, which is removed\n",
    "first by fitting the wings.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`spectrum()`** is a plain averaged power spectrum of a captured record, for the band survey."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  ANALYSIS\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "def sweep(freqs, drive_frac=None, navg=None, settle=None, level_guard=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Drive at each frequency and read the complex response at DC.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns (f_actual, z) where f_actual is what the generator really produced\n",
    "    (its word is quantised) and z is complex - amplitude AND phase.\n",
    "\n",
    "    The receiver is tuned by WORD, not by hertz, so the signal lands at exactly\n",
    "    zero frequency and the two register reads cannot land on different phases of\n",
    "    a rotating vector.\"\"\"\n",
    "    drive_frac = DRIVE_FRAC if drive_frac is None else drive_frac\n",
    "    navg = N_AVG if navg is None else navg\n",
    "    settle = SETTLE if settle is None else settle\n",
    "\n",
    "    gen.amp(drive_frac)                  # refused outright if above DRIVE_MAX\n",
    "    gen.run()\n",
    "    f_act = np.zeros(len(freqs))\n",
    "    z = np.zeros(len(freqs), dtype=complex)\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        for k, f in enumerate(freqs):\n",
    "            f_act[k] = gen.freq(f)\n",
    "            acq.tune_word(gen.lo_word())\n",
    "            time.sleep(settle)\n",
    "            if level_guard is not None and sc.peak_frac(1024) > level_guard:\n",
    "                raise RuntimeError('input exceeded %.0f%% of full scale at %.6f MHz'\n",
    "                                   % (100 * level_guard, f_act[k] / 1e6))\n",
    "            z[k] = acq.measure(navg)\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        # Whatever ended this sweep - the guard above, a bad register read, a\n",
    "        # Ctrl-C halfway through a 350-point pass - the drive comes off. This is\n",
    "        # the single most important line in the notebook: every measurement goes\n",
    "        # through here, so no failure path can walk away leaving the coil driven.\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "    return f_act, z\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fit_lorentzian(f, p, guard=0.05, minpts=5):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Centre, linewidth, peak and baseline from power p against frequency f.\n",
    "\n",
    "    1/p is a parabola in f for a PURE Lorentzian. Any additive floor is absorbed\n",
    "    into that parabola and widens the answer, so the floor is found by search:\n",
    "    for each trial floor, subtract it, fit, rebuild the full model, and keep the\n",
    "    trial that reproduces the measured points best. Two passes, coarse then fine.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Points below `guard` of the peak are excluded - their reciprocals are all\n",
    "    noise - and the rest are weighted by their power, so the well-measured points\n",
    "    near the top dominate.\"\"\"\n",
    "    f = np.asarray(f, dtype=float)\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(p, dtype=float)\n",
    "    pmax = float(np.max(p))\n",
    "    u = f - f.mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _try(b):\n",
    "        q = p - b\n",
    "        keep = q > guard * q.max()\n",
    "        if int(np.count_nonzero(keep)) < minpts:\n",
    "            return None\n",
    "        A, B, C = np.polyfit(u[keep], 1.0 / q[keep], 2, w=q[keep])\n",
    "        if A <= 0.0:\n",
    "            return None                              # parabola opens the wrong way\n",
    "        u0 = -B / (2.0 * A)\n",
    "        lw = 2.0 * np.sqrt(max(C / A - u0 ** 2, 1e-30))\n",
    "        p0 = 1.0 / max(C - A * u0 ** 2, 1e-300)\n",
    "        f0 = f.mean() + u0\n",
    "        model = p0 / (1.0 + (2.0 * (f - f0) / lw) ** 2) + b\n",
    "        rms = float(np.sqrt(np.mean(((p - model) / pmax) ** 2)))\n",
    "        return rms, (f0, lw, p0, b)\n",
    "\n",
    "    best, best_b = _try(0.0), 0.0\n",
    "    hi = 0.999 * float(np.min(p))\n",
    "    if hi > 0.0:\n",
    "        for b in np.linspace(0.0, hi, 17):\n",
    "            got = _try(b)\n",
    "            if got is not None and (best is None or got[0] < best[0]):\n",
    "                best, best_b = got, b\n",
    "        w = hi / 16.0\n",
    "        for b in np.linspace(max(best_b - w, 0.0), min(best_b + w, hi), 17):\n",
    "            got = _try(b)\n",
    "            if got is not None and (best is None or got[0] < best[0]):\n",
    "                best, best_b = got, b\n",
    "    if best is None:\n",
    "        raise ValueError('fit failed: only %d points above the guard'\n",
    "                         % int(np.count_nonzero(p > guard * p.max())))\n",
    "    resid = best[0]\n",
    "    f0, lw, p0, base = best[1]\n",
    "    return dict(f0=f0, lw=lw, peak=p0, base=base, resid=resid, Q=f0 / lw)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def width_from_phase(f, z, f0_hint, lw_hint, tau_max=2.0e-6, ngrid=81):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Linewidth from the PHASE alone - independent of every amplitude effect.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Why this is worth having: the amplitude fit's weakness is an additive floor\n",
    "    under the peak, which inflates the width. The phase does not know about the\n",
    "    floor, or about the gain, or about the drive drifting - so if the two agree,\n",
    "    neither is being fooled by any of those.\n",
    "\n",
    "    The complication is that a fixed transport delay (cables, the coil's leads,\n",
    "    the converters) adds a straight ramp to the phase, and near the centre of\n",
    "    the line a ramp is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a change of linewidth. Fitting the\n",
    "    ramp from the wings does not work either: the resonator's own phase is\n",
    "    antisymmetric about the centre, so a straight line through both wings eats a\n",
    "    large part of the swing being measured.\n",
    "\n",
    "    So both are fitted together, against the full model\n",
    "\n",
    "        phase(f) = c - 2 pi tau (f - f0) - arctan( 2 (f - f0) / lw )\n",
    "\n",
    "    by a two-dimensional grid search over the delay and the linewidth. The\n",
    "    constant c falls out as a mean at each trial, so only two parameters are\n",
    "    searched and the whole thing is a few thousand vector operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns (linewidth, delay_seconds, residual_degrees), or (None, None, None)\n",
    "    if the swing is too small to fit.\"\"\"\n",
    "    f = np.asarray(f, dtype=float)\n",
    "    ph = np.unwrap(np.angle(np.asarray(z)))\n",
    "    df = f - f0_hint\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Normalise the direction of the swing: the model below is written for a\n",
    "    # phase that FALLS with frequency, which is the usual convention, but the\n",
    "    # sign that arrives depends on the mixer and on the cabling.\n",
    "    if np.polyfit(f, ph, 1)[0] > 0:\n",
    "        ph = -ph\n",
    "        flip = -1.0\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        flip = 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    if np.ptp(np.degrees(ph)) < 30.0:\n",
    "        return None, None, None          # not enough swing to fit anything\n",
    "\n",
    "    lws = lw_hint * np.linspace(0.4, 2.5, ngrid)\n",
    "    taus = np.linspace(0.0, tau_max, ngrid)\n",
    "\n",
    "    best = None\n",
    "    for lw in lws:\n",
    "        arc = np.arctan(2.0 * df / lw)\n",
    "        for tau in taus:\n",
    "            model = -2.0 * np.pi * tau * df - arc\n",
    "            r = ph - model\n",
    "            r = r - np.mean(r)           # the constant c, solved exactly\n",
    "            cost = float(np.mean(r ** 2))\n",
    "            if best is None or cost < best[0]:\n",
    "                best = (cost, lw, tau)\n",
    "\n",
    "    cost, lw_fit, tau_fit = best\n",
    "    # Refuse an answer that has run into the edge of the search: it means the\n",
    "    # true value is outside the grid, and the number returned would be the\n",
    "    # boundary rather than a measurement.\n",
    "    if lw_fit <= lws[1] or lw_fit >= lws[-2]:\n",
    "        return None, None, None\n",
    "    return lw_fit, tau_fit * flip, float(np.degrees(np.sqrt(cost)))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def spectrum(z, f_out, navg=8):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Averaged power spectrum of a complex record. Returns (offset_hz, power).\n",
    "\n",
    "    The record is split into navg segments, each windowed and transformed, and\n",
    "    the power spectra averaged - which trades frequency resolution for a much\n",
    "    steadier floor. Offsets are relative to the local oscillator, and negative\n",
    "    offsets mean BELOW it.\"\"\"\n",
    "    n = len(z) // navg\n",
    "    if n < 16:\n",
    "        raise ValueError('record too short for %d averages' % navg)\n",
    "    win = np.hanning(n)\n",
    "    acc = np.zeros(n)\n",
    "    for k in range(navg):\n",
    "        seg = z[k * n:(k + 1) * n] * win\n",
    "        acc += np.abs(np.fft.fftshift(np.fft.fft(seg))) ** 2\n",
    "    acc /= navg * (np.sum(win ** 2) * n)\n",
    "    return np.fft.fftshift(np.fft.fftfreq(n, d=1.0 / f_out)), acc\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('analysis helpers defined')"
   ]
  },
