    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 5 — A second, independent width\n",
    "\n",
    "On the emulator, Q was known. Here nothing is, so the discipline that replaces it is\n",
    "**measuring the same quantity two ways that fail differently**. If they agree, the number is\n",
    "probably right. If they disagree, something is loading the coil, compressing it, or sitting in\n",
    "the band — and you have learned that before building anything on top of it.\n",
    "\n",
    "**5a — the phase.** Free: it comes from the sweep already taken. A resonator's phase swings\n",
    "through 180° across its line, and how *fast* it swings is set by the linewidth. It uses **no\n",
    "amplitude information at all**, which is precisely why it is a good check on a method that is\n",
    "entirely about amplitude — a sloping baseline, a drifting drive level or a wrong gain cannot\n",
    "touch it.\n",
    "\n",
    "One complication has to be handled rather than ignored. Cables, leads and converters add a\n",
    "fixed transport delay, which puts a straight ramp on the phase — and near the centre of the\n",
    "line a ramp looks exactly like a change of linewidth. They cannot be separated locally, and\n",
    "they cannot be separated by fitting the wings either, because the resonator's own phase is\n",
    "antisymmetric about the centre and a straight line through both wings would absorb much of the\n",
    "swing being measured. So the delay and the linewidth are fitted **together**, which costs a\n",
    "small grid search and hands back the loop's transport delay as a bonus — a number Step 8 has\n",
    "no other way of knowing.\n",
    "\n",
    "**5b — the ring-down.** Genuinely independent: a *time-domain* measurement of the same physics.\n",
    "Drive the coil, cut the drive, watch the decay. The time constant is `Q / (π f₀)` — about 1.4 µs\n",
    "at Q = 180 and 40 MHz.\n",
    "\n",
    "That speed is the whole difficulty. The decimated chain is far too slow — the entire event fits\n",
    "inside one output sample — so this must be done on the raw scope path. And the drive is cut\n",
    "from Python, whose timing jitter is tens of microseconds, so the record has to be long enough\n",
    "for the switch-off to land somewhere inside it and the edge is then **found** rather than\n",
    "assumed. That is what the decimation ladder is for.\n",
    "\n",
    "The routine refuses to report a number it cannot support: too few points across the decay, too\n",
    "little contrast, or no edge found, and it says so instead."
   ]
  },
