    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 8 — Feedback against a real coil\n",
    "\n",
    "The flagship measurement, on hardware that is no longer pretending. Feedback takes the coil's\n",
    "own signal, shifts its phase, scales it and adds it back, which changes two things about the\n",
    "resonator: the **quality factor** (feedback aligned with the coil's motion cancels part of its\n",
    "loss) and the **centre frequency** (feedback aligned with the coil's displacement acts like\n",
    "changing the tuning).\n",
    "\n",
    "Three things are different from every previous stage, and all three are handled by measuring\n",
    "rather than assuming:\n",
    "\n",
    "**1. The phase axis is not meaningful in absolute terms.** The loop now runs through cables,\n",
    "connectors and the coil itself, adding delay the phase shifter's latency correction cannot\n",
    "know about. So the two special phases are *found*, and everything is reported relative to\n",
    "them. A fixed offset in the phase axis is expected and is not an error.\n",
    "\n",
    "**2. There is no overload flag.** The emulator's sticky clip bit has quietly been the guard\n",
    "for ten stages and it is gone. Every point below checks the raw input level first and abandons\n",
    "the point rather than fitting nonsense.\n",
    "\n",
    "**3. Self-oscillation is approached, not entered.** Past a certain gain the loop's net loss\n",
    "goes negative and the coil sustains itself. On the emulator that was safe and bisecting to the\n",
    "boundary was a measurement. Here the loop saturates the input instead, and a saturated input\n",
    "produces a distorted shape that still looks vaguely like a resonance — this project's\n",
    "signature failure. So the boundary is **extrapolated** from the linear region and deliberately\n",
    "not walked into. Entering it should be a separate, deliberate experiment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 8a - THE PHASE AXIS: find the two special phases\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 8 - feedback on the real coil')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "acq.start(DEC_USE)\n",
    "whole, frac = ps.config_delay(F0)\n",
    "print('quarter-period delay line: %d whole clocks + %.3f' % (whole, frac))\n",
    "print('probing %d phases at gain %.2f' % (len(FB_PHASES), FB_GAIN_PROBE))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "grid8 = F0 + np.linspace(-3.0, 3.0, 31) * LW     # wider: feedback moves the line\n",
    "\n",
    "fb_phi, fb_q, fb_df = [], [], []\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    for phi in FB_PHASES:\n",
    "        ps.set(FB_GAIN_PROBE, phi)\n",
    "        time.sleep(SETTLE)\n",
    "        gen.freq(F0); gen.amp(DRIVE_FRAC); gen.run(); time.sleep(0.02)\n",
    "        lvl = sc.peak_frac(1024)\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "        if lvl > FB_LEVEL_GUARD:\n",
    "            print('  %4d deg : ABANDONED, input at %.2f of full scale' % (phi, lvl))\n",
    "            fb_phi.append(phi); fb_q.append(np.nan); fb_df.append(np.nan)\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            f8, z8 = sweep(grid8, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=32,\n",
    "                           level_guard=FB_LEVEL_GUARD)\n",
    "            gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "            fit8 = fit_lorentzian(f8, np.abs(z8) ** 2)\n",
    "            fb_phi.append(phi); fb_q.append(fit8['Q']); fb_df.append(fit8['f0'] - F0)\n",
    "            print('  %4d deg : Q = %7.1f  (x%.2f),  centre %+8.1f Hz (%+.3f lw)'\n",
    "                  % (phi, fit8['Q'], fit8['Q'] / Q_SWEEP, fb_df[-1], fb_df[-1] / LW))\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            fb_phi.append(phi); fb_q.append(np.nan); fb_df.append(np.nan)\n",
    "            print('  %4d deg : fit failed (%s)' % (phi, exc))\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    # The feedback loop is closed while this runs. Any exception, or\n",
    "    # a Ctrl-C between two phases, must not leave it that way.\n",
    "    ps.off()\n",
    "    gen.off()\n",
    "\n",
    "fb_phi = np.array(fb_phi, dtype=float)\n",
    "fb_q = np.array(fb_q, dtype=float)\n",
    "fb_df = np.array(fb_df, dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "if np.all(~np.isfinite(fb_q)):\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError('every feedback point failed - check levels and coupling')\n",
    "\n",
    "PHI_NARROW = float(fb_phi[int(np.nanargmax(fb_q))])\n",
    "PHI_BROAD = (PHI_NARROW + 180.0) % 360.0\n",
    "PHI_SHIFT = float(fb_phi[int(np.nanargmax(np.abs(fb_df)))])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('  narrowing phase (max Q)      : %.0f deg  (Q x %.2f)'\n",
    "      % (PHI_NARROW, np.nanmax(fb_q) / Q_SWEEP))\n",
    "print('  broadening phase (opposite)  : %.0f deg' % PHI_BROAD)\n",
    "print('  largest centre shift at      : %.0f deg (%+.0f Hz)'\n",
    "      % (PHI_SHIFT, fb_df[int(np.nanargmax(np.abs(fb_df)))]))\n",
    "_sep = (PHI_SHIFT - PHI_NARROW) % 360.0\n",
    "print('  separation between them      : %.0f deg' % _sep)\n",
    "if min(abs(_sep - 90.0), abs(_sep - 270.0)) > 35.0:\n",
    "    print('  WARNING: the two effects should be a quarter turn apart. They are')\n",
    "    print('  not, which usually means the fits are noisy or the loop is already')\n",
    "    print('  compressing. Lower FB_GAIN_PROBE and repeat before reading on.')"
   ]
