    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 9 — Close the loop on the instrument, and write down what was learned\n",
    "\n",
    "Two things happen here, in this order.\n",
    "\n",
    "**First, the self-test is run again.** If it passed at the start and passes now, nothing about\n",
    "the instrument changed while you were measuring the coil — so the numbers below are about the\n",
    "coil. If it passed then and fails now, the coil measurements are not trustworthy and the\n",
    "reason is in the board, not the physics. This is the one check that no amount of care with the\n",
    "coil can substitute for, and it costs ten seconds.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Then everything measured is written to a file**, so the next notebook does not have to be\n",
    "told the answer by hand. That was the one thing the emulator made free and a real coil does\n",
    "not: `reso.config()` used to be read back in about forty places. Now there is a file instead."
   ]
